Proposal for API/API worker security definitions.

Security definitions are defined at the API level, with routes and workers opting into named security definitions, from their parent API.

potential example:
```typescript
import { api } from "@nitric/sdk";

// example auth0 issuer configuration
const public = api('public', {
  security: {
     'client': api.JWTAuthorizer({
        issuer: 'https://YOUR-ACCOUNT-NAME.auth0.com',
        audiences: ['test']
     })
  }
});

// Not sure on the best way we could reflect this for the API routes
// example here looks pretty messy
api.get('/test', async ctx => {
  
}, {
  // map to the above authorizer by name
  security: 'client'
});
```

This PR connects the stake page to the stablejoe and moneymaker subgraphs:
- APR calculated based on USD remitted ;
- Fee calculation has not changed ;
- Moved remittances table below the charts ;

We are still using the bar subgraph to populate the fee chart
